1
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:38,760
Makes sense, right?

2
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:42,000
You get it, right?

3
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,920
I know, I know.

4
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:47,900
If you get it, shut up and follow me!

5
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:02,520
There's a turtle over there!

6
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:05,880
I'm sure there's a turtle!

7
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:07,660
It's really autumn now

8
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,280
If there is...

9
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:14,820
Hey, Ebisu!

10
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:19,020
Isn't that Ebisu? Long time no see.

11
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:21,300
Yotsu-senpai.

12
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:22,900
What are you laughing at?

13
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:24,480
Did something good happen?

14
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:27,960
Actually, I'm unemployed right now.

15
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,840
I've been so down, not knowing what to do.

16
00:01:33,580 --> 00:01:35,220
Don't act depressed while laughing.

17
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:37,660
Hahahaha!

18
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:40,920
As usual, you're a real laughing stock.

19
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,800
Hahahaha!

20
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:44,540
Knock it off already.

21
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:47,400
By the way, you said you quit the police,

22
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:51,480
but weren't you scouted by the Special
Investigation Division after that?

23
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:53,180
Hahahaha!

24
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:54,300
Well, you see...

25
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:55,420
Hahahaha!

26
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:01,320
Don't you dare come any closer!

27
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:03,040
Get a car ready.

28
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,500
Don't try to be slick.

29
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:11,400
Who's the bastard who's angry?!

30
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:15,760
Because nowadays you go around
wearing a Restroyer mask like that,

31
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:20,060
you're not going to bring out God-nee-chan and the rest,
are you?

32
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:23,360
Hey! Don't laugh!

33
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:26,080
Maybe Magi Mineko is around too.

34
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,440
Kichimome and so on.

35
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:31,040
Damn it! I'll shoot!

36
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:32,600
"I'll shoot," he says!

37
00:02:34,380 --> 00:02:37,220
Don't tell me you know this is a model gun?

38
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:40,500
A model gun, he says.

39
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:42,860
Either way, didn't you know?

40
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:46,840
You're one of us now too.

41
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,640
Because it's a model gun, you see!

42
00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:52,220
The hostage is laughing at him.

43
00:02:56,060 --> 00:02:56,940
Now!

44
00:02:58,180 --> 00:03:01,400
Kaipan Deka, now joining the fray!

45
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:08,820
Nice work, you comedy cop!

46
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:16,300
"Comedy cop." That's a great nickname

47
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:19,600
I actually kind of liked it too.

48
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,900
Then there was no need to quit, was there?

49
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:24,520
It's fine when I'm out on the job,

50
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:31,160
but I have to face those special
detectives every single day.

51
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:38,680
I laughed so hard every day that my abs twisted,
and I was hospitalized many times.

52
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:44,720
I see. Not even several bodies
would hold up under that.

53
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:49,520
Senpai, this is my house.
Would you like to stop in for some tea?

54
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:52,100
What? Motoshoku Ebisu Shrine?

55
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,640
So your home is a shrine?

56
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:57,896
Yes, it was built by Tokugawa Ieyasu,

57
00:03:57,946 --> 00:04:02,560
and it's a historic shrine that the
Ebisu family has protected for generations.

58
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:14,380
Whoa, what's with all these statues?

59
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:16,654
They're all statues of Ebisu.

60
00:04:16,704 --> 00:04:19,580
It's a collection my ancestors
gathered over generations.

61
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:24,240
Some of them are supposedly worthy of being
designated Important Cultural Properties.

62
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:27,580
Is it this big,
shiny gold one in the middle?

63
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,940
That one belonged to my grandfather,
but it's just plated.

64
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:33,340
I'll go make some tea.

65
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:34,760
Thanks.

66
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:38,020
So this is the plated one.

67
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:42,060
Which one is the Ebisu worthy of
being an Important Cultural Property?

68
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:44,340
This one?

69
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:49,320
It's heavy, but it's got a sulky face.
It's not a cheerful Ebisu face.

70
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:53,740
This one looks especially old.

71
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:57,000
Achoo!

72
00:04:58,580 --> 00:04:59,160
Whoa!

73
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:01,540
Uh-oh!

74
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:07,780
Damn, this is bad.
I'll have to take them home and fix them.

75
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:11,040
There are so many of them.

76
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:14,960
If I leave them like this,
they probably won't notice for now.

77
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:15,540
Senpai!

78
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:18,120
What are you doing?

79
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:21,840
No, no, no, Ebisu-sama is a
god who brings good luck, right?

80
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:25,260
I was praying,
hoping to share in his blessings.

81
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:30,860
You're the type who'd trample
a god to get what you want.

82
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:35,040
Hey, don't laugh.

83
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:37,580
S-sorry, senpai, tea...

84
00:05:37,580 --> 00:05:42,060
Sorry, I just remembered some work,
so I'm heading home.

85
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:44,740
Senpai has work?

86
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:48,100
W-weird...

87
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:53,560
I'll just head home quietly today.

88
00:05:57,700 --> 00:06:01,060
Okay, so if I do it like this...

89
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:06,680
This should fool them somehow.

90
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:10,400
Then I just need to quietly put them back.

91
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:19,140
What's with that crowd over there?

92
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:22,100
What happened?

93
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:24,840
Apparently, the Ebisu statues were stolen.

94
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:25,540
What?

95
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:28,560
Ryotsu-senpai.

96
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:28,980
Gulp.

97
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:29,840
Senpai...

98
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:31,700
I didn't steal them!

99
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:35,300
What are you talking about?

100
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:39,240
There are a hundred Ebisu statues. There's
no way one person could steal them all.

101
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:41,180
Come on.

102
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:43,740
Did they really steal all of
them without anyone noticing?

103
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:45,200
That's right.

104
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:46,200
We're in real trouble.

105
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:47,900
Is this a laughing matter?

106
00:06:48,460 --> 00:06:49,460
Sorry.

107
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:55,720
Anyway, the statue I smashed
managed to avoid getting smashed.

108
00:06:57,640 --> 00:06:59,440
Ebisu-san has really been through it,
hasn't he?

109
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:01,140
But it's strange.

110
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:04,580
There was a safe nearby, too.

111
00:07:04,580 --> 00:07:07,120
Apparently that one wasn't touched at all.

112
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:09,760
So only the Ebisu statues were stolen?

113
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:11,880
Yeah, that does seem odd.

114
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:15,920
Could the culprit be a thief who
specializes in Buddhist statues and art?

115
00:07:18,660 --> 00:07:20,960
That stolen Ebisu statue...

116
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:22,700
Apparently it was found
on the railway tracks.

117
00:07:22,700 --> 00:07:23,840
What?!

118
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:33,000
No doubt about it,
they're all our Ebisu statues.

119
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:40,860
I have no idea. Some of them are solid gold,
worth a million, and even Important Cultural Property grade.

120
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:42,940
Why would the culprit throw them away?

121
00:07:42,940 --> 00:07:47,660
Anyway, senpai,
why are you carrying a banana?

122
00:07:48,140 --> 00:07:49,760
I was on my way to throw it out.

123
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:53,060
What's wrong, Reiko-san?

124
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:55,960
Look at this.
Holes have been drilled into it.

125
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:03,340
Sure enough, every one of them has its
base gouged out and holes bored into it.

126
00:08:03,780 --> 00:08:05,340
What could this mean?

127
00:08:06,220 --> 00:08:07,020
I wonder.

128
00:08:07,940 --> 00:08:08,740
That's strange.

129
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:15,700
What's wrong, Ryo-chan?

130
00:08:16,860 --> 00:08:20,340
No, I just had a feeling
someone was watching us.

131
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:22,220
Must be my imagination.

132
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:30,780
Anyway, I'm just glad our
precious Ebisu-sō came back safe.

133
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:42,240
That guy, he's not to be trusted.

134
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:46,020
Damn it.

135
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:50,600
Maybe I should've just slipped it
in with the others in the chaos.

136
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:54,220
W-what's this?

137
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:58,360
Found it.

138
00:09:01,980 --> 00:09:03,760
This is an old map.

139
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:04,660
What does it say?

140
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:09,900
When the waterfall's water runs dry,
the key to Ura-Edo Castle will be unlocked.

141
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,160
What is this?

142
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:15,020
What do you think, Nakagawa?

143
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:17,300
I have no idea at all.

144
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:21,580
Is "when the waterfall's water
runs dry" some kind of metaphor?

145
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:24,620
I wonder if a waterfall could ever run dry.

146
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:27,160
And what's this
"Ura-Edo Castle" supposed to be?

147
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:28,620
Do you know anything about it?

148
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:29,460
Well...

149
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:31,080
I've never heard of it.

150
00:09:31,680 --> 00:09:32,282
I see,

151
00:09:32,332 --> 00:09:35,920
I thought Nakagawa or
Reiko might know something.

152
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:39,600
Then why don't you ask
Deiemon-san in 4-chome?

153
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:41,100
That's a good idea.

154
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:43,500
Deiemon-san is famous as a local historian,

155
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:45,440
so he might be able to figure something out.

156
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:52,700
H-hey, this is a major discovery!

157
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:55,020
Don't suddenly shout like that.

158
00:09:55,420 --> 00:09:57,260
What's the major discovery?

159
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:00,460
This was written by Ieyasu.

160
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:00,880
What?

161
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:04,620
Look, both the handwriting
and the face are Ieyasu's.

162
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:05,500
No way.

163
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:10,340
It's true. There's a photo of a letter
Ieyasu wrote to one of his retainers.

164
00:10:10,340 --> 00:10:13,660
The face drawn there is
exactly like Ieyasu's.

165
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:15,880
Look.

166
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:17,720
Let's see, let's see...

167
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:20,540
Hey, isn't this Yamaharu's photo book?

168
00:10:20,540 --> 00:10:22,660
What? I-I grabbed the wrong one.

169
00:10:24,260 --> 00:10:25,020
This one.

170
00:10:25,020 --> 00:10:26,640
Don't put them together!

171
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:27,720
Look.

172
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:31,240
It's identical!

173
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:35,020
There's no doubt about it,
Ieyasu himself wrote this!

174
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:37,980
And the map was tucked away

175
00:10:37,980 --> 00:10:40,360
inside this Ebisu statue, you know.

176
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:43,400
The shrine that kept these,
the Ganso Ebisu Shrine,

177
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:47,100
said it was a prestigious
shrine built by Ieyasu.

178
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:48,260
I see.

179
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
This might just be a treasure map!

180
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,340
Treasure? Where?

181
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:57,200
This is just my own deduction, but

182
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:59,840
after Ieyasu won the Battle of Sekigahara,

183
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:05,060
you know he destroyed the Toyotomi clan in
the Winter and Summer Sieges of Osaka, right?

184
00:11:05,060 --> 00:11:07,880
You've seen it in NHK dramas and movies,
haven't you?

185
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:13,340
Apparently, Ieyasu secretly moved
the treasure out of Edo Castle.

186
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:16,540
Wait a minute.

187
00:11:16,540 --> 00:11:17,800
Could that be...

188
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:20,020
the one Shigesato Itoi
is searching for on TV?

189
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:21,880
The Tokugawa buried gold?

190
00:11:21,880 --> 00:11:22,860
Probably.

191
00:11:22,860 --> 00:11:26,160
So how much is that buried gold worth?

192
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:27,400
Well, let's see.

193
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:30,500
It was enough war funding
to take back the realm,

194
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:32,980
so converted to today's money,

195
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:35,580
it's probably about one trillion yen.

196
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:40,620
One trillion yen.

197
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:42,400
One trillion yen

198
00:11:44,060 --> 00:11:46,180
So where exactly is it hidden?

199
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:48,440
This map alone isn't enough, though.

200
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:52,520
There are probably several maps, and we won't
get anywhere unless we have them all together.

201
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:55,500
Isn't the treasure buried right here?

202
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:57,560
It can't be that simple, can it?

203
00:11:57,560 --> 00:12:00,520
If it were that easy,
we wouldn't have had to struggle this much.

204
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:04,740
W-who the hell are you?

205
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:08,160
Hand over that map and
the Ebisu statue quietly.

206
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:10,740
Hand them over, and I'll spare your life.

207
00:12:10,740 --> 00:12:11,500
What'd you say?

208
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:14,780
Who am I, you idiot!

209
00:12:15,740 --> 00:12:19,000
Looks like I have no choice
but to take it by force.

210
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:24,460
Hand it over quietly!

211
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:26,140
Heh, you're naive!

212
00:12:32,020 --> 00:12:32,900
Damn you!

213
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:34,060
What?

214
00:12:35,460 --> 00:12:37,060
You, you did it now!

215
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:40,960
W-what's this?

216
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:48,900
I thought it was a history book,
but it's all idol photo books!

217
00:12:48,900 --> 00:12:51,020
Stop, that's my collection!

218
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:54,180
What are you gawking at? Hurry up and do it!

219
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:01,360
Stop it!

220
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:07,080
Don't you dare! That's a photo
book I worked hard to collect!

221
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:08,240
That one...

222
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:13,040
Stop! That's a premium item!

223
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:13,980
This one?

224
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:17,280
- Showdown!
- Showdown!

225
00:13:17,780 --> 00:13:21,260
Yaa! Riot!

226
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:23,760
- Aaah!
- Halt!

227
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:25,900
- Me! Me!
- Me!

228
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:28,480
That one trillion yen is mine!

229
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:31,160
Yay!

230
00:13:37,300 --> 00:13:38,740
They're fast...

231
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:40,180
They're like ninjas.

232
00:13:45,140 --> 00:13:48,800
Just as Sasukebei suspected,
they're a formidable opponent.

233
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:49,640
Yes.

234
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:53,280
Listen,
gather the data on that man right away.

235
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:54,620
Understood.

236
00:13:58,840 --> 00:13:59,880
One trillion yen.

237
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:03,460
Is there really that much gold buried?

238
00:14:03,460 --> 00:14:04,560
No doubt about it.

239
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:10,240
Considering we've already had our lives threatened
by that mysterious ninja army after the buried gold.

240
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:13,940
But how are we supposed to search with
just this map and the Ebisu statue?

241
00:14:13,940 --> 00:14:16,660
Don't worry, I've got a lead.

242
00:14:16,660 --> 00:14:18,500
We're going into action starting tomorrow.

243
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:20,280
Wait a minute, senpai.

244
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:20,960
What is it?

245
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:23,880
What about our work?

246
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:27,720
Idiot! How can you search for buried gold if you're
scared of getting docked for unauthorized absence?

247
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:28,560
No way...

248
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:32,900
Once we succeed,
I'll give each of you 100 billion yen.

249
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:34,460
That's 100 billion yen, you know!

250
00:14:35,220 --> 00:14:38,820
Even when you say that, the amount
is so huge it just doesn't sink in.

251
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:42,540
You're all such hopeless paupers.

252
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:43,320
Listen up.

253
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:45,280
With 100 billion yen,

254
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:48,240
we could buy the whole company

255
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:49,600
that makes your favorite Documemo!

256
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:50,180
What?

257
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:52,620
You'd become president on the spot,

258
00:14:52,620 --> 00:14:55,820
and you could rewrite the
Documemo scripts however you like

259
00:14:55,820 --> 00:15:00,000
and do all sorts of things with Saori!

260
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:03,820
All sorts of things with Saori...

261
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:07,960
Bolbo!

262
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:13,660
Take half of the hundred billion
yen to Colonel Babullyu as a dowry.

263
00:15:13,660 --> 00:15:17,140
Do that, and he'll say yes to
you marrying Jodie right away.

264
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:18,800
Marriage?

265
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:24,700
Then you can do all sorts of
things with Jodie every night!

266
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:28,460
All sorts of things with Jodie...

267
00:15:32,060 --> 00:15:32,860
Honda.

268
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:33,500
Yes?

269
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:40,640
You can buy as many luxury bikes as you want,
the Ducatis and BMWs you've been wanting for ages!

270
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:45,760
Really? That's amazing!

271
00:15:47,440 --> 00:15:53,940
So, senpai, what kind of all
sorts of things will I get to do?

272
00:15:53,940 --> 00:15:56,340
Figure that out yourself.

273
00:15:56,340 --> 00:15:58,040
Just as I thought.

274
00:15:58,980 --> 00:16:03,440
Anyway, we'll be free of this daily
grind of working ourselves to the bone.

275
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:05,420
You'll go along with this, right?

276
00:16:10,060 --> 00:16:13,620
Why'd you dress up in
such a ridiculous getup?

277
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:17,160
The enemy's ninjas, so we're a ninja squad.

278
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:19,680
Anyway, there's something I want to ask you.

279
00:16:20,900 --> 00:16:21,700
What is it?

280
00:16:21,700 --> 00:16:27,180
Are there other shrines like this one, with
"Ganso" in the name, that enshrine the Seven Lucky Gods?

281
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:34,860
There are six more across the Kanto region,
like Ganso Benzaiten Shrine and Ganso Fukurokuju Shrine.

282
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:36,840
Can you find those places right away?

283
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:38,800
Yes, I can.

284
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:42,620
These are the places with the seven shrines,
including this one.

285
00:16:42,620 --> 00:16:46,040
Let's see, which one is closest from here?

286
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:50,100
Here it is. Ganso Benzaiten Shrine.

287
00:16:50,100 --> 00:16:51,280
Alright, let's go.

288
00:16:51,280 --> 00:16:53,380
That won't be necessary.

289
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:04,400
Who are you? I'm Haruka Benten, the only daughter
of the Ganso Benzaiten Shrine you're looking for.

290
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:07,440
Nice to meet you, pleased to meet you.

291
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:12,620
You're quite my type.

292
00:17:17,080 --> 00:17:22,020
That's... senpai, this one, sis,
could you let me see that for a moment?

293
00:17:22,020 --> 00:17:26,500
Sure. It's similar in
construction to the Ebisu statue.

294
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:29,340
There's a hole open right there.

295
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:33,040
N-nothing!

296
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:36,620
Hey, wasn't there an old
map or something inside this?

297
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:39,100
Could it be this?

298
00:17:39,780 --> 00:17:42,600
So it was in there after all? Let me see it.

299
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:42,680
She's even more my type.

300
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:45,820
There's the same Kao here too!

301
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:48,697
Let's see...
When the Seven Lucky Gods are all gathered,

302
00:17:48,747 --> 00:17:51,480
the door to the keep of the
hidden Edo Castle will open.

303
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:53,560
Hidden Edo Castle again?

304
00:17:54,420 --> 00:17:55,520
What's that?

305
00:17:55,520 --> 00:17:58,360
This has nothing to do with you.
Don't stick your nose in.

306
00:17:59,060 --> 00:18:02,000
You're done here, so you can go home now.

307
00:18:02,780 --> 00:18:04,680
Hurry up and go home. Shoo, shoo.

308
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:06,660
Yeah, yeah, I get it.

309
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:13,000
Was there ever such a cute girl
at the Ganso Benzaiten Shrine?

310
00:18:14,080 --> 00:18:15,180
Well, never mind.

311
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:18,000
Um, your name was Haruka-chan, right?

312
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:18,460
Yes.

313
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:20,628
About this Benten statue and the map,

314
00:18:20,678 --> 00:18:23,680
could you lend them to us for a while?

315
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:24,580
No way.

316
00:18:26,080 --> 00:18:30,320
It's not fair to try to hog Ieyasu
Tokugawa's buried treasure all for yourselves.

317
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:32,660
Gulp! How did you know that?

318
00:18:32,660 --> 00:18:37,720
There's a real Ieyasu face on it too, so anyone could
figure it out if they just thought about it for a bit.

319
00:18:37,720 --> 00:18:39,220
I see.

320
00:18:39,220 --> 00:18:44,880
I found the map inside this a week ago,
and I've been looking into things ever since.

321
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:47,740
What a clever little girl.

322
00:18:48,580 --> 00:18:51,980
Don't tell me you guys
have a similar map too,

323
00:18:51,980 --> 00:18:55,500
and you figured there must be six more,
since it's the Seven Lucky Gods?

324
00:18:55,980 --> 00:18:58,560
Wow, you see right through us.

325
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:01,900
That's exactly what I thought too,
which is why I came to visit here.

326
00:19:02,340 --> 00:19:04,580
Hey, let me join in too!

327
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:10,020
Can't be helped,
our shares will shrink a little,

328
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:12,540
but we'd better team up at this point.

329
00:19:12,540 --> 00:19:13,900
Listen up, you lot.

330
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:14,180
Yes!

331
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:16,760
Yay!

332
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:20,720
Now then, on to the Ganso Benzaiten Shrine,
let's go, let's go!

333
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:21,380
Okay, okay.

334
00:19:21,380 --> 00:19:23,320
Wow, she's a handful, isn't she.

335
00:19:25,980 --> 00:19:27,340
Let's go!

336
00:19:30,060 --> 00:19:31,280
What was stolen?

337
00:19:31,280 --> 00:19:36,380
Three days ago, a group dressed like
suspicious ninjas broke in on us.

338
00:19:36,380 --> 00:19:40,200
They made off with Lord Benzaiten herself.

339
00:19:40,640 --> 00:19:43,080
It's them, damn it, they beat us to it!

340
00:19:44,900 --> 00:19:48,600
I almost had this Ebisu
statue taken from me too.

341
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:53,700
Can't be helped. Let's try the next one,
the Ganso Fukurokuju Shrine.

342
00:19:53,700 --> 00:19:55,640
That's a waste of time.

343
00:19:55,640 --> 00:19:59,140
At the shrines with
"Ganso" in their names that enshrine the Seven Lucky Gods,

344
00:19:59,140 --> 00:20:02,400
apart from the Benzaiten
and Daikokuten shrines,

345
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:06,580
the main deities have all been
stolen within the past week.

346
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:07,880
What?!

347
00:20:09,320 --> 00:20:12,300
We have Ebisu and Benzaiten, two of them.

348
00:20:13,020 --> 00:20:15,361
The enemy has Bishamonten, Fukurokuju,

349
00:20:15,411 --> 00:20:18,600
Jurojin, and Hotei, four in all?

350
00:20:19,420 --> 00:20:20,680
What should we do, Ryotsu?

351
00:20:21,140 --> 00:20:23,905
Since only Daikokuten seems to be safe,

352
00:20:23,955 --> 00:20:26,440
let's go to the Ganso Daikokuten Shrine!

353
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:29,960
Honda, take out the map you got from Ebisu!

354
00:20:30,300 --> 00:20:30,660
Yes!

355
00:20:31,580 --> 00:20:32,260
Got it!

356
00:20:33,060 --> 00:20:33,600
This is it!

357
00:20:45,780 --> 00:20:48,960
What is this, all high-end residences?

358
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:52,000
Is there really a shrine around here?

359
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:53,200
Over there.

360
00:20:54,860 --> 00:20:57,760
What is that? That's not a shrine.

361
00:20:57,760 --> 00:21:04,020
The chief priest of the Ganso Daikokuten Shrine, I suppose,
being the one who enshrines Daikoku, the god of business prosperity,

362
00:21:04,020 --> 00:21:05,940
is a total businessman.

363
00:21:05,940 --> 00:21:11,180
He made a fortune in stocks and land deals,
and five years ago he shut the shrine down.

364
00:21:12,300 --> 00:21:12,440
What?

365
00:21:12,820 --> 00:21:14,940
Ahahahaha!

366
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:19,384
Yes, so,

367
00:21:19,434 --> 00:21:24,140
I was wondering if we might borrow that
Daikoku statue for just a little while.

368
00:21:24,140 --> 00:21:25,220
No way!

369
00:21:25,940 --> 00:21:28,853
To someone like you,
some nobody from who knows where,

370
00:21:28,903 --> 00:21:31,020
there's no way I'd lend out Lord Daikokuten!

371
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:33,120
Come on, please, just this once!

372
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:34,540
It's useless! Just get lost!

373
00:21:35,900 --> 00:21:37,300
What's with that face?!

374
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:39,660
Hey, just because you don't get it back,

375
00:21:39,710 --> 00:21:41,980
don't you dare come sneaking in to steal it!

376
00:21:42,660 --> 00:21:45,874
Actually, last night some
suspicious gang broke in too,

377
00:21:45,924 --> 00:21:49,460
but our security system
gave them a thorough beating!

378
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:52,460
Those guys ran off with
their tails between their legs!

379
00:21:55,500 --> 00:21:56,520
Damn it!

380
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:00,180
How did it go, senpai?

381
00:22:00,180 --> 00:22:02,080
No good, he won't hear any of it.

382
00:22:02,080 --> 00:22:04,000
What are we going to do, Ryotsu?

383
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:06,440
Well then, what should we do?

384
00:22:09,220 --> 00:22:12,060
So, senpai, what exactly are we going to do?

385
00:22:14,540 --> 00:22:17,920
First, we sneak in from
the sky using a hang glider.

386
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:20,100
That's trespassing, you know!

387
00:22:20,100 --> 00:22:22,580
Then we blow the door off with a grenade.

388
00:22:22,580 --> 00:22:24,120
That's property damage!

389
00:22:24,120 --> 00:22:26,660
Then we put Daikoku to
sleep with hypnosis gas.

390
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:29,280
That's a total crime, isn't it?

391
00:22:29,280 --> 00:22:31,560
We're just borrowing it for a bit.

392
00:22:31,560 --> 00:22:32,400
No way!

393
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:33,540
What?

394
00:22:33,540 --> 00:22:34,780
What is it?

395
00:22:34,780 --> 00:22:42,360
I'm a ninja.

396
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:43,380
Are they the ones?

397
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:51,480
Who goes there?

398
00:23:00,460 --> 00:23:02,980
What a rowdy bunch.

399
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:13,020
At this rate,
they'll steal the Daikoku statue!

400
00:23:13,020 --> 00:23:15,160
Let's go, Senpai Ryo!

401
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:21,520
Are you all right?

402
00:23:21,520 --> 00:23:22,360
Senpai.

403
00:23:22,360 --> 00:23:23,660
It hurts.

404
00:23:23,660 --> 00:23:24,840
The door...

405
00:23:24,840 --> 00:23:26,040
It's open.

406
00:23:26,040 --> 00:23:28,240
Perfect, we're going in!

407
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:30,080
This is bad, man.

408
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:30,880
Shut up.

409
00:23:30,880 --> 00:23:34,060
We're police officers who
happened upon a crime scene.

410
00:23:34,060 --> 00:23:35,180
We can't just leave it alone.

411
00:23:35,780 --> 00:23:37,020
Such a convenient

412
00:23:37,020 --> 00:23:37,800
Let's go.

413
00:23:45,700 --> 00:23:46,420
What's wrong?

414
00:23:46,840 --> 00:23:48,540
The ninjas are gone.

415
00:23:48,540 --> 00:23:50,360
How dare you do this to us!

416
00:23:50,360 --> 00:23:52,280
Wait! We're the police!

417
00:23:52,280 --> 00:23:54,400
We rushed over after hearing the commotion.

418
00:23:54,400 --> 00:23:56,260
Is there such a thing as
a police officer like that?

419
00:23:56,260 --> 00:23:56,980
Go!

420
00:24:08,260 --> 00:24:10,360
Something's making a racket outside.

421
00:24:10,820 --> 00:24:11,900
Good evening.

